# Hugeicons Pro (@hugeicons-pro/*) ships from Hugeicons' own registry, not npmjs.
# The web app uses the solid-rounded set for the same glyphs the RN app fills in
# (see components/ui/Icon.tsx → SOLID_ICON_MAP).
#
# The token is read from the environment, and uses the SAME variable name as
# mobile/.npmrc so one export covers both installs. Set HUGEICONS_NPM_TOKEN
# locally and in the Vercel project's environment variables so `npm install` can
# resolve the package at build time. Never paste the literal token here — this
# file is committed.
@hugeicons-pro:registry=https://npm.hugeicons.com
//npm.hugeicons.com/:_authToken=${HUGEICONS_NPM_TOKEN}
